                :retrieved "refs/friston2016.pdf"}
  :friston2018bmr {:cite "Friston, K., Parr, T., & Zeidman, P. (2018). Bayesian model reduction. arXiv:1805.07092."
                   :used-for "Bayesian model reduction: evidence change for a reduced model, used by structure learning"
                   :verified {:eq9 "F[P̃:P] = ln E_Q[P̃(θ)/P(θ)] + F[P]: log evidence of the reduced model" :table1 "closed forms; Dirichlet row" :text "p. 617 region: a reduced model is accepted when its log-evidence gain is greater than zero (the paper's ΔF is reduced minus full)"}
                   :sign-convention "The War Machine's ΔF (Holes.lean modelReductionFreeEnergyChange; bmr.clj) is ln B(A) + ln B(a′) − ln B(a) − ln B(A′), which is the NEGATIVE of the paper's reduced-minus-full log evidence, i.e. ΔF_WM = ln P(y|full) − ln P(y|reduced). Verified numerically 2026-09-01: identical rows give ΔF_WM = −5.01, paper +5.01. Hence 'accept when ΔF_WM ≤ −3' means the reduced model wins by ≥ 3 nats."
                   :retrieved "refs/friston2018bmr.pdf"}
  :kass1995 {:cite "Kass, R. E., & Raftery, A. E. (1995). Bayes factors. Journal of the American Statistical Association, 90(430), 773-795."
