  {:id :precision :defines :Pi :node :R7 :class :theory-defined :ref :buckley2017
   :imports [:eps :eps0]
   :formal "Pi_k := 1 / max(Var(eps_k), eps0)" :eq nil :lean nil :lean-status :missing
   :note "Var(eps_k) is the bounded rolling variance of channel k's prediction ERROR history (precision.clj:116-135 update-channel-precision: production precision is the variance component of new-error; the observation enters only the separately emitted :salience term under the default :salience-mode :separate). Earlier this row imported :o and said 'variance of o_k' -- corrected 2026-09-01 (C10, found reviewing D5f): at symbol grain R7 imports eps, so the theory edge is R8->R7, and R2->R7 holds only at route grain. In buckley2017 eq. 45 the variances σ are model parameters, not sample statistics; this row is therefore stack-defined in content and only theory-defined in role." :code "precision.clj:116-135, 160-190; war_machine.clj:4380-4388"}
